{"G1054":{"id":"G1054","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1054","disambiguated_id":"G1054 = a Spelling of","unique_id":"G1053","headword":"Γαλατικός","transliteration":"Galatikos","lexical_morphology":"N:A--LG","gloss_en":"Galatia","definition_en":"Γαλατικός, -ή, -όν (see previous word), \n Galatian, belonging to Galatia: Act.16:6 18:23.†\n (AS)","source_line":1179}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"gálata","count":1},{"gloss":"da-Galácia","count":1}]},"G1357":{"id":"G1357","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1357","disambiguated_id":"G1357 =","unique_id":"G1357","headword":"διόρθωσις","transliteration":"diorthōsis","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"reformation","definition_en":"διόρθωσις, -εως, ἡ (see supr.), \n __1. a making straight. \n __2. a reforming, reformation (used in late writers of laws, etc.): Heb.9:10 (Cremer, 807).†\n διόρθωμα, -τος, τό\n (διορθόω, to make straight, set right), \na correction, reform: Act.24:3.†\n διόρθωσις, -εως, ἡ (see supr.), \n __1. a making straight. \n __2. a reforming, reformation (used in late writers of laws, etc.): Heb.9:10 (Cremer, 807).†\n (AS)","source_line":1489}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"retificação","count":1}]},"G1392":{"id":"G1392","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1392","disambiguated_id":"G1392 =","unique_id":"G1392","headword":"δοξάζω","transliteration":"doxazō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to glorify","definition_en":"δοξάζω\n (δόξα), [in LXX chiefly for כָּבַד ni., pi., also for פָּאַר, etc. ;] \n__1. to think, suppose, hold an opinion (Æsch., Plat., al.). \n __2. To bestow δόξα (which see) on, to magnify, extol, praise (Thuc., iii, 45; Plut., al.): with accusative, Mat.5:16, Mrk.2:12, Jhn.8:54, Rom.15:6, 1Pe.2:12, al.; id. before ἐπί Luk.2:20; ἐν, Gal.1:24, 1Pe.4:16. \n __3. In LXX and NT (see: δόξα, 3), to clothe with splendour, glorify (Exo.34:29-30, Psa.37:20, Isa.44:23, Est.3:1, al): Rom.8:30, 2Co.3:10, 2Th.3:1, 1Pe.1:8, al.; of Christ, Jhn.7:39 8:54, al. (on the Johannine use, see Cremer, 211; Westc., Jo., Intr.); of the Father, Jhn.13:31-32, 1Pe.4:11, al. (cf. ἐν-, συν-δοξάζω). \n (AS)","source_line":1524}],"occurrence_count":61,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"glorificado","count":10},{"gloss":"glorificaram","count":6},{"gloss":"glorificavam","count":5},{"gloss":"glorificando","count":4},{"gloss":"glorifica","count":4},{"gloss":"foi-glorificado","count":4},{"gloss":"glorificou","count":4},{"gloss":"glorifiquem","count":3},{"gloss":"glorificará","count":3},{"gloss":"glorifique","count":2},{"gloss":"glorificaria","count":2},{"gloss":"honrados","count":1},{"gloss":"honra","count":1},{"gloss":"glorificava","count":1},{"gloss":"glória","count":1},{"gloss":"glorifico","count":1},{"gloss":"glorificarei","count":1},{"gloss":"glorifiquei","count":1},{"gloss":"glorifiqueis","count":1},{"gloss":"então","count":1},{"gloss":"caso","count":1},{"gloss":"que-foi-glorificado","count":1},{"gloss":"glorificarão","count":1},{"gloss":"glorificada","count":1},{"gloss":"glorioso","count":1}]},"G1793":{"id":"G1793","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1793","disambiguated_id":"G1793 =","unique_id":"G1793","headword":"ἐντυγχάνω","transliteration":"entugchanō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to call on","definition_en":"ἐν-τυγχάνω \n [in LXX: Da TH Dan.6:12-13 (קֶרֶב) Wis.8:20 16:28, 2Ma.2:25 2Mac 4:36 2Mac 6:12 2Mac 15:39, 3Ma.6:37; before κατά, 1Ma.8:32 1Mac 10:61-64 1Mac 11:25 * ;] \n__1. to fall in with. \n __2. to meet with in order to converse. \n __3. to petition, make petition: with dative of person(s), before ὑπέρ with genitive of person(s), Act.25:24 (cf. Field, Notes, 140), Heb.7:25, Rom.8:27, 34 (θεῷ, not expressed); before κατά, against: Rom.11:2 (cf. ἔντευξις, ὑπερ-εντυγχάνω).†\n (AS)","source_line":1934}],"occurrence_count":5,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"intercede","count":2},{"gloss":"recorreu","count":1},{"gloss":"fala","count":1},{"gloss":"interceder","count":1}]},"G1799":{"id":"G1799","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1799","disambiguated_id":"G1799 =","unique_id":"G1799","headword":"ἐνώπιον","transliteration":"enōpion","lexical_morphology":"G:PREP","gloss_en":"before","definition_en":"ἐνώπιος, -ον\n (ὤψ), [in LXX for פָּנִים, etc. ;] \nface to face, in sight (Theocr.; ἄρτοι ἐ., Exo.25:29): neut., ἐνώπιον, in vernacular, with force of prep. with genitive [in LXX for פָּנִים, עַיִן, etc., cf. Dalman, Words, 31 f., 209 f., and Deiss., BS., 213], in NT, most frequently in Lk, Ac, Re, never in Mt, Mk, before, in the presence of: Luk.1:19 Luk.4:7, Act.4:10 Act.6:5, Rev.1:4 2:14, al.; esp. ἐ. Κυρίου (θεοῦ), in the sight of God, or with God as witness or as judge, Rom.14:22, 1Co.1:29, 1Ti.2:3, Jas.4:10, 1Pe.3:4, al. \n (AS)","source_line":1940}],"occurrence_count":94,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"diante","count":86},{"gloss":"presença","count":6},{"gloss":"diante-de","count":1},{"gloss":"na-presença","count":1}]},"G2281":{"id":"G2281","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2281","disambiguated_id":"G2281 =","unique_id":"G2281","headword":"θάλασσα","transliteration":"thalassa","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"sea","definition_en":"θάλασσα, -ης, ἡ \n [in LXX chiefly for יָם ;] \nthe sea: Mat.23:15, Mrk.11:23, Luk.21:25, Rom.9:27, Heb.11:12, Jas.1:6, Ju 13, Rev.7:1, al.; τὸ πέλαγος τῆς θ. (see Tr., ut infr.), Mat.18:6; ὁ οὐρανὸς κ. ἡ γῆ κ. ἡ θ., of the whole world, Act.4:24, al. (Hag.2:7); θ. ὑαλίνη, Rev.4:6 15:2; of the Mediterranean, Act.10:6, 32 17:14; of the Red Sea, ἐρυθρὰ θ., Act.7:36, 1Co.10:1-2, Heb.11:20; of an inland lake (as Heb. יָם), θ. τ. Γαλιλαίας, Mat.4:18 15:29, Mrk.1:16 7:31; τ. Τιβεριάδος, Jhn.21:1; τ. Γ. τ. T., Jhn.6:1; of the same, simply ἡ θ., Mat.4:15, Mrk.2:13, al \n SYN.: πέλαγος, the vast expanse of open water\"; θ., \"the sea as contrasted with the land\" (Tr., Syn., xiii) (AS)","source_line":2430}],"occurrence_count":91,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"mar","count":90},{"gloss":"do-mar","count":1}]},"G269":{"id":"G269","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0269","disambiguated_id":"G0269 =","unique_id":"G0269","headword":"ἄμαχος","transliteration":"amachos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"peacable","definition_en":"ἄμαχος, -ον\n (μάχη); \n__1. invincible (frequently in cl.). \n __2. abstaining from fighting, non-combatant (Xen.). Metaphorical (cf. MM, VGT, see word), not contentious: 1Ti.3:3, Tit.3:2.†\n (AS)","source_line":372}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"sim","count":1},{"gloss":"briguentos-sim","count":1}]},"G3342":{"id":"G3342","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3342","disambiguated_id":"G3342 =","unique_id":"G3342","headword":"μεταξύ","transliteration":"metaxu","lexical_morphology":"G:PREP","gloss_en":"between/meanwhile","definition_en":"μεταξύ\n (μετά + ξύν = σύν), [in LXX: Gen.31:50, Jdg.5:27, III Ki 15:6; 3Ki.15:32, Wis.4:10 16:19 18:23 * ;] \n__1. adv. of place and time (in NT time only); \n __(a) between: ἐν τῷ μ. (s.with χρόνῳ), Jhn.4:31; \n __(b) in late writers (FlJ, Plut., al.), like μετά (adv.), after, afterwards: τὸ μ. σάββατον, Act.13:42 (cf. Cl., Ro., I Co., 44, 2). \n __2. Prep. with genitive, between: of place, Mat.23:35, Luk.11:51 16:26, Act.12:6; of persons, as to mutual relation, Mat.18:15, Act.15:9, Rom.2:1-29 15:1-33.†\n (AS)","source_line":3455}],"occurrence_count":9,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"entre","count":7},{"gloss":"seguinte","count":1},{"gloss":"os-pensamentos","count":1}]},"G3400":{"id":"G3400","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3400","disambiguated_id":"G3400 =","unique_id":"G3400","headword":"μίλιον","transliteration":"milion","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"mile","definition_en":"a Roman mile, milliarium , = 1000 paces,= 8 stades, = 1680 yards, i. e. 80 yards less than our mile, (Polybius Historicus), etc. (ML)","source_line":3513}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"milha","count":1}]},"G3733":{"id":"G3733","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3733","disambiguated_id":"G3733 =","unique_id":"G3733","headword":"ὄρνις","transliteration":"ornis","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"hen","definition_en":"ὄρνις, -ιθος, ὁ, ἡ \n [in LXX: ὄ. ἐκλεκταί, I2Ki.3:1 4:23 (3Ki.5:3) (בַּרְבֻּר)* ;] \na bird; specif., a cock, a hen: Mat.23:3, Luk.13:34 (WH).†\n (AS)","source_line":3850}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"ajunta","count":1},{"gloss":"galinha","count":1}]},"G3922":{"id":"G3922","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3922","disambiguated_id":"G3922 =","unique_id":"G3922","headword":"παρεισέρχομαι","transliteration":"pareiserchomai","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to come in","definition_en":"παρ-εισ-έρχομαι \n __1. to come in beside or by the way: Rom.5:20. \n __2. to come in secretly, steal in: Gal.2:4.†\n (AS)","source_line":4040}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"entrou","count":1},{"gloss":"infiltrado","count":1}]},"G3993":{"id":"G3993","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3993","disambiguated_id":"G3993 =","unique_id":"G3993","headword":"πένης","transliteration":"penēs","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"poor","definition_en":"πένης, -ητος, ὁ\n (πένομαι, to work for one's daily bread), [in LXX for אֶבְיוֹן, עָנִי, דַּל, etc. ;] \none who works for his living, a labourer, a poor man: 2Co.9:9.†\n SYN.: πτωχός, properly a beggar and implying deeper poverty than π. (see Tr., Syn., § xxxvi, Abbott, Essays, 78) (AS)","source_line":4115}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"pobres","count":1}]},"G4031":{"id":"G4031","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4031","disambiguated_id":"G4031 =","unique_id":"G4031","headword":"περικρατής","transliteration":"perikratēs","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"in control of","definition_en":"περι-κρατής, -ές \n [in LXX: Da TH Sus 1:39 A * ;] \nhaving full command of: Act.27:16.†\n (AS)","source_line":4153}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"senhores","count":1}]},"G4492":{"id":"G4492","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4492","disambiguated_id":"G4492 =","unique_id":"G4492","headword":"ῥιζόω","transliteration":"rhizoō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to root","definition_en":"ῥιζόω, -ῶ\n (ῥίζα), [in LXX: Isa.40:24, Jer.12:2 (שָׁרַשׁ), Sir.3:28 24:12 * ;] \nto cause to take root. Metaphorical, to plant, fix firmly, establish: pass. (EV, rooted), ἐν ἀγάπῃ, Eph.3:18(17); ἐν Χριστῷ, Col.2:7 (cf. ἐκ ριζόω).†\n (AS)","source_line":4625}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"enraizados","count":1},{"gloss":"raízes","count":1}]},"G4610":{"id":"G4610","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4610","disambiguated_id":"G4610 = a Name of","unique_id":"G4609","headword":"Σιλουανός","transliteration":"Silouanos","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Silvanus","definition_en":"Σιλουανός\n (in MSS also Σιλβανός, a form frequently in π.), -οῦ, ὁ, \nSilvanus, latinized name of Silas: 2Co.1:19, 1Th.1:1, 2Th.1:1, 1Pe.5:12.†\n (AS)","source_line":4748}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Silvano","count":4}]},"G47":{"id":"G47","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0047","disambiguated_id":"G0047 =","unique_id":"G0047","headword":"ἁγνεία","transliteration":"hagneia","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"purity","definition_en":"ἁγνεία (WH, ἁγνία), \n [in LXX for טָהֳרָה, נָזִיר, נֶזֶר, etc. ;] \npurity: 1Ti.4:12, 5:2 (Cremer, 58. For exx. of ceremonial use in π., see MM, Exp., iv).†\n (AS)","source_line":142}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"pureza","count":2}]},"G4755":{"id":"G4755","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4755","disambiguated_id":"G4755 =","unique_id":"G4755","headword":"στρατηγός","transliteration":"stratēgos","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"officer/magistrate","definition_en":"στρατηγός, -οῦ, ὁ\n (στραός, ἄγω), [in LXX chiefly for סָגָן (always in pl.), שַׂר ;] \n__1. a military commander, a general (Hdt., al.). \n __2. A civic commander, a governor, magistrate (Hdt., Xen., al.): Act.16:20, 22 16:35-36, 38. \n __3. The commander of the Levitical guard of the Temple, ὁ σ. τ. ἱεροῦ (EV, captain of the Temple): Act.4:1 5:24, 26; pl., Luk.22:4, 52.†\n SYN.: ἄρχων (cf. EGT on Act.16:20; Ramsay, St. Paul, 217). (AS)","source_line":4903}],"occurrence_count":10,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"magistrados","count":4},{"gloss":"oficiais","count":3},{"gloss":"guarda","count":2},{"gloss":"oficial","count":1}]},"G4932":{"id":"G4932","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4932","disambiguated_id":"G4932 =","unique_id":"G4932","headword":"συντέμνω","transliteration":"suntemnō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to cut short","definition_en":"συν-τέμνω \n [in LXX chiefly for חָרַץ ;] \n__1. to cut in pieces. \n __2. to cut down, cut short: metapb., λόγον, Rom.9:28 (LXX) (Hdt., Plat., Fur., al.).†\n (AS)","source_line":5084}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"abreviando","count":1}]},"G501":{"id":"G501","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0501","disambiguated_id":"G0501 =","unique_id":"G0501","headword":"ἀντλέω","transliteration":"antleō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to draw","definition_en":"ἀντλέω, -ῶ\n (ἄντλος, bilge-water in a hold), [in LXX for שָׁאַב, etc. ;] \n__1. prop., to bale out. \n __2. Generally, to draw water: absol., Jhn.2:8 4:15; ὕδωρ, Jhn.2:9 4:7 (on its use of the water made wine, see DCG, ii, 815a; MM, VGT, see word; Field, Notes, 84 f.).†\n (AS)","source_line":609}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"tirar","count":2},{"gloss":"tirai","count":1},{"gloss":"tinham-tirado","count":1}]},"G5312":{"id":"G5312","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5312","disambiguated_id":"G5312 =","unique_id":"G5312","headword":"ὑψόω","transliteration":"hupsoō",